JSP 815 pack: content licence
=============================

1. Attribution statement

Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government
Licence v3.0.

2. Source identification

Source 1, the Framework:
  JSP 815: Defence Safety Management System (SMS) Framework, V1.3,
  published 2026-09-01, Ministry of Defence, © Crown copyright.

Source 2, the Direction and Guidance volume:
  JSP 815: Defence Safety Management System (SMS) Direction and Guidance,
  V1.3 (includes Annex H at V1.2), published 2026-09-01, Ministry of
  Defence, © Crown copyright.

3. Source links

Framework publication page (P1):
https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/defence-safety-management-system-jsp-815-part-1
Direction and Guidance publication page (P2):
https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/defence-safety-management-system-jsp-815-volume-2
Collection page (P0):
https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/defence-safety-management-system-jsp-815

Both publication pages carry the gov.uk footer sentence: "All content is
available under the Open Government Licence v3.0, except where otherwise
stated" (pages fetched 2026-09-25).

4. Licence

Open Government Licence v3.0:
https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/

5. Nature of this pack

This pack contains reconstructed reference notes, not reproductions. Content
was restructured and summarised from the source; passages are paraphrased
except short defined terms.

6. Non-endorsement

Nothing in this pack suggests that the Ministry of Defence endorses it or
that it has any official status.

7. Excluded material

The following material is excluded from the licence grant and is not
reproduced in this pack:
- ISO 45001 clause text quoted in Annex F. The pack carries clause numbers
  only, per the Annex F mapping.
- Third-party passages quoted in the source: the HSE definition of safety
  culture (Element 1), the HSE definition of competence (Element 6), the
  MOD-HSE Memorandum of Understanding passage on RIDDOR reporting
  (Element 10), and the ISO 19011 Annex B audit technique list (Element 12).
- MOD crests and logos, and military insignia.
- Annex G Assurance Toolkit (spreadsheet).

8. Scope

This licence governs the content of this pack (SKILL.md, chapters/,
glossary.md, cheatsheet.md). The repository's MIT licence covers tooling and
scaffolding only.

9. Per-source record

One block per attachment used in the build (20 of the 21 published
attachments; the spreadsheet in section 7 gets no block). "Used in" names
this pack's chapters (ch01 to ch10).

